  "summary": "French colonial architecture adapted to tropical and subtropical climates with distinctive local features.",
  "description": "Features wide verandas, steep roofs, and French elements blended with Caribbean and Creole influences, particularly in Louisiana.",
  "culturalContext": "French colonial building — from Caribbean plantation houses through Pondicherry's quarters to Hanoi's Indochinese villas — adapted French Beaux-Arts and Provençal habits to colonial climates with arcaded ground floors, louvered verandas and later tropical modernist experiments. Hanoi's French Quarter, Saigon's Opera and Dakar's plateau districts show the range; decolonization turned many administrative ensembles into national landmarks and conservation battlegrounds.",
